      "message": "feat(machine): machine files name a default holder for new tools\n\nOptional tooling.spindle_mount (BT30/BT40/CAT40/TTS) and\ntooling.default_holder (a built-in holder-library entry) in a .mch,\nrefused by name at the reader, the Machines pane validator and a\nproject's stored machine: unknown mount or holder, a non-word, a holder\noff the stated mount. A NEW tool added in the GUI or through MCP\nadd_tool on a machine stating a default starts with that holder's drawn\nprofile in the add's own undo step (AddTool::with_holder, sharing\nSetToolBody::library's body builder); a stated holder wins; a default\nthe tool's shank cannot take is left off with a named note. Existing\ntools and documents never change. The Tormach MX mills state BT30 /\nBT30 ER20, the PCNC and M mills TTS / TTS ER20 (public source:\ntormach.com/tormach_mills). MCP add_tool takes \"holder\" and reports the\nholder it landed with; load_machine shows both keys.\n\nFixes #828\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
