      "message": "fix(tools): a machine-default holder never judges looser than the stand-in cylinder\n\nReview-fix round on PR #880 (maintainer's rule, 2026-11-11):\n\n- An ASSUMED holder (the machine's tooling.default_holder landed on a new\n  tool) is judged by the union of its drawn bands and the tool's\n  holder_d x holder_len cylinder (HolderProfile::floored, applied in\n  tool_body::judged). A holder picked explicitly keeps its real shape.\n- ToolBody::machine_default records which: set only by AddTool's default\n  door inside the add's undo step; saved as an additive\n  \"machine_default\": true key on the tool body (absent = explicit, so\n  older files' holders count as picked); a term in the op stamp.\n- Pinned on BT30 and TTS: the band 55-65 mm above the tip, 20 mm off the\n  axis - the default convicts where the bare tool does, the explicit pick\n  is judged by its nut/collar.\n- camcraft-post no longer depends on camcraft-tools (maintainer reversal):\n  the post reader takes a HolderLookup from its caller; the app passes\n  machine::holder_lookup and shadows parse_mch / tooling_refusals.\n- A stored default holder that no longer resolves is refused naming\n  tooling.default_holder.\n- Decision record and test comment no longer claim \"stricter\".\n\nRefs #828\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
